From 647432fe2717bb1e0236cd0b557449257d68c932 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mir Mohammad Sajedul Islam <mohammad.sajedul.islam@g.bracu.ac.bd>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 06:30:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Secure the API and add subscription management for the
 admin

Security
- Every admin route now requires a signed-in admin; the old open admin
  endpoints are gone. Admin is the is_admin flag, an ADMIN role, or the
  address in ADMIN_EMAIL (default rabbi@edutrack.com).
- Lectures, study sheets and the AI tutor need an active subscription.
- Token signing key can no longer be the published default; it comes from
  SECRET_KEY, or is derived from DATABASE_URL so restarts keep sessions.
- Login attempts are throttled and server errors no longer leak details.
- File upload is closed. Study sheets are Google Drive links, lectures are
  YouTube links, both validated and normalised.

Subscriptions
- Cash renewals recorded with days, optional amount and note, kept in a
  payment history. Double taps are rejected and the latest payment can be
  undone. Renewing extends from the current end date if still running.
- Status per student: active, expiring (7 days or fewer), expired, pending.
- In-app warnings at 7, 3 and 1 days left, plus expiry and renewal notes.

Admin data
- Overview totals, attention list, batches, content and AI usage, and cash
  recorded this month.
- Student detail with progress per subject and chapter, streak, recent
  activity and payment history.
- Unpublished lectures and sheets stay visible to the admin.

Tests cover the above (73 passing).
